# @hsk-sync:note-meta

Token `@hsk-sync:note-meta` marks shared **note title / note date** resolution.

Python source of truth is `harrix_pylib.note_meta`. This repo re-exports it from `harrix_pyssg.note_meta`.

If priority, parsing rules, or date formats change, update the sibling implementations and consider how generated HTML titles and note UIs will look.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| Python (pylib, source of truth) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-pylib\src\harrix_pylib\note_meta.py` |
| Python (this repo, re-export) | `src/harrix_pyssg/note_meta.py` (+ `Article.generate_html` title) |
| VS Code (JS) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\note-meta.js` |
| Android (Kotlin) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-android` — `NoteMetaResolver.kt`, `NoteTitleExtractor.kt` |

## Shared contract

### Title (`resolve_note_title`)

1. YAML `title:`
2. Else first `#` heading
3. Else `title_from_id(file_stem)` (part after `__`, `-`/`_` → spaces, title case)
4. Else `Untitled`

### Date (`resolve_note_date`)

1. Date fragment in file name
2. Else YAML `date:`
3. Else file ctime
4. Else file mtime

Keep `tests/test_note_meta.py` in sync with behavior changes.
